<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1931" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">al-lĕvio</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adl-</span></b> ), āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		lĕvis, = allĕvo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make light</i>, <i>to lighten.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut (navis) alleviaretur ab eis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Jonas, 1, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib. Act. 27,
			38</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to raise up</i>, <i>relieve</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alleviabit eum Dominus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Jac. 5, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">curas alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just. Nov. Const. 13</span></i>
			.—Spec.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alleviata est terra Zabulon,</span>”
				<i>is dealt lightly</i>, <i>leniently with</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 9, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
